# UNLOCK — Security

When security/trust boundaries are relevant:
- derive authoritative identity from trusted server authentication;
- authentication does not replace authorization;
- fail closed on unresolved permission semantics;
- keep secrets/service/database credentials server-only;
- avoid raw SQL/stack/secret leakage in client responses;
- authenticate before privileged DB/runtime construction where the architecture requires it;
- do not add RLS automatically; current baseline uses explicit server-side authorization unless an accepted task/decision says otherwise;
- do not mutate hosted state or expose `.env.local` values.

Use canonical auth/API docs/rules for details.
